turn5search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; REVISITING GAMMA CONJECTURE I: COUNTEREXAMPLES AND MODIFICATIONS\n\nSERGEY GALKIN, JIANXUN HU, HIROSHI IRITANI, HUAZHONG KE, CHANGZHENG LI, AND ZHITONG SU\nREVISITING GAMMA CONJECTURE I: COUNTEREXAMPLES AND MODIFICATIONS\n\nSERGEY GALKIN, JIANXUN HU, HIROSHI IRITANI, HUAZHONG KE, CHANGZHENG LI, AND ZHITONG SU\n\n**Abstract.** We continue investigation of asymptotics of quantum differential equation for Fano manifolds, with a special regard to Gamma conjecture I and its underlying Conjecture O. We introduce the A-model conifold value, a symplectic invariant of a Fano manifold, and propose modifications for Gamma conjecture I based on this new definition. We discuss an interplay of birational transformations with an extension of Gamma conjecture I over the Kähler moduli space. These heuristics are applied to rigorously identify the principal asymptotic class in the case of \\(\\mathbb{P}^1\\)-bundles \\(X_n = \\mathbb{P}_{\\mathbb{P}^n}(\\mathcal{O}\\oplus \\mathcal{O}(n))\\). We observe, in particular, that for \\(X_n\\) of dimension at least four, the Conjecture O holds just for even values of \\(n\\), and in these cases we falsify the original non-modified Gamma conjecture I.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIzv. Akad. Nauk SSSR (https://www.mathnet.ru/links/02b55acc43f73f0546bcf6679d2122d8/im2210_eng.pdf)\nciteturn5search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.4 years ago; GALKIN ... we give examples and counterexamples.\n2 \nV. M. GALKIN\nR), and by the same token the study of £;(s) reduces to the study of the zeta-functions\nof local rings. In §2 we present information concerning the structure of the ideals in\nthese rings.\nIn §3 we introduce a Hausdorff topology on R. The completion !R of the field R\nis a locally compact ring. The closure U of the ring A = I is compact in it. We com-\npute some integrals which are necessary for what follows. In §4 we give a